## Statement

Simplify $\sqrt{3+2\sqrt2}$.

## Hint

Look for integers $a,b$ with $(a+b\sqrt2)^2=3+2\sqrt2$.

## Solution

We compute $(1+\sqrt2)^2=1+2\sqrt2+2=3+2\sqrt2$.

Since $1+\sqrt2>0$, the square root of $(1+\sqrt2)^2$ is $1+\sqrt2$. Hence
$$\sqrt{3+2\sqrt2}=1+\sqrt2.$$
